  - convert to final boolean with threshold 0.5.
- Add one more conservative correction rule on top of the average:
  - if the variants strongly disagree, use the median probability instead of the mean,
  - this reduces the impact of one noisy refit.
- A practical merge recipe:
  - collect `p1, p2, p3` from 3 refits,
  - set `p_mean = (p1 + p2 + p3) / 3`,
  - set `p_med = median([p1, p2, p3])`,
  - final_prob = `0.7 * p_mean + 0.3 * p_med`,
  - predict `final_prob > 0.5`.
