  - it keeps the original pipeline intact,
  - it avoids exposing fragile probability-access assumptions,
  - it uses a true ensemble effect from model instability rather than a second learner on top of hard labels.
- To make the merge more robust without much extra code, use a “confidence-weighted vote”:
  - weight each model by its validation accuracy on its own holdout,
  - normalize weights to sum to 1,
  - average probabilities with these weights.
